TI  - Molecularly orchestrated room-temperature phosphorescent biocomposite for intelligent food packaging: Integrating anti-counterfeiting and real-time visual freshness supervision
T2  - FOOD PACKAGING AND SHELF LIFE
LA  - English
KW  - Polyvinyl alcohol/chitosan
KW  - Food packaging
KW  - Food preservation
KW  - Anti-counterfeiting
KW  - FILMS
KW  - ALIZARIN
AB  - Addressing the global challenge of food spoilage and counterfeiting requires next-generation intelligent packaging that synergizes active preservation, security, and real-time monitoring. This study pioneers a roomtemperature phosphorescent smart bio-based film (B-CPA-BOH) engineered to transcend conventional packaging by integrating triple functionalities: robust anti-counterfeiting, food freshness preservation, and visual realtime spoilage supervision. Constructed from biodegradable polyvinyl alcohol/chitosan (CS/PVA) substrates, the film achieves orchestrated multifunctionality through molecular design: alizarin confers pH-responsive visual freshness monitoring with intrinsic antibacterial/antioxidant capacity, while 9-Phenanthreneboronic acid (9-PhBA) enables ultralong Phosphorescent lifetime (1.75 s) for anti-counterfeiting and 3D information encryption. Surface modification with beeswax establishes a superhydrophobic barrier (water contact angle: 113.3 degrees), significantly enhancing moisture resistance. As a sustainable alternative to polyethylene (PE) films, B-CPA-BOH extends food shelf life by 2 days while enabling smartphone-visualized freshness tracking. The persistent atmospheric-stable phosphorescence permits sophisticated optical encryption through programmable afterglow patterning, while functioning synergistically as a hygroscopicity indicator. A breakthrough dual-mode detection platform emerges through smartphone coupling, where progressive acid-base chromism visually tracks microbial proliferation while customized room-temperature phosphorescent (RTP) signatures authenticate product integrity. This molecularly orchestrated system redefines intelligent packaging paradigms by concurrently overcoming three industry-critical limitations: vulnerability to biological contamination through active bioprotection, susceptibility to forgery via information encryption, and information opacity through consumeraccessible visual analytics. Demonstrated through successful prototype testing, the fully biodegradable film establishes a sustainable blueprint for next-generation smart packaging, directly contributing to circular economy objectives through waste stream reduction, resource efficiency, and supply chain security enhancement.
